        2485
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Accordingly, the Committee recommends that the City adopt the afore-mentioned practices that have proven successful over the years in private industry. We also recommend that the City specify in its furniture bids and purchase contracts the following: \"The Vendor shall not employ in the delivery, unloading and installation of furniture any man or means whose employment may cause strike, stoppage or other similar troubles by workmen employed either by the Contractor, his subcontractors, by other contractors or their subcontractors, or by other workmen whose services might affect the progress of the work on the site where the furniture is to be delivered and installed.\"",
